Lift these {{ transition_count }} validated concrete forward transition(s) into
one portable candidate SkillCard hypothesis. Return exactly one JSON object
with intent, anchor, carrier, preconditions (array), effects (array), risks
(array), requires/provides/conflicts (arrays of {locus, name}), and "scope" as
{cases, languages, platforms, prior_actions}. Copy applicable case, language,
and platform identifiers from the input context; do not invent hardware names.
Use stable semantic loci and mechanism names shared with the transitions.
requires lists needed code features; provides lists introduced features;
conflicts lists incompatible or already-present features at the same locus.
The carrier must remain actionable and code-bearing, while intent is abstract.
Keep tuning choices in the carrier; one card describes one semantic transformation.
Include failure evidence in risks. Do not claim held-out verification or gains
without measurements. The example illustrates granularity, not a required skill.

